{
 "about": [
  "R-113 (the owner's ruling at Story 4.10's test, 2026-09-15): the settings-panel group of every setting the design export declares, by category and by the row title a design's panel prints.",
  "Made from the export's own category specs (the reconciled state of each design's Controls), classified by two independent passes against the rule in docs/section-authoring.md § 2, each disagreement settled into that rule's words, then swept once more for one group per kind across categories.",
  "A value is the group; an object carries the group most designs use and, under designs, the design numbers whose setting of that title does something else.",
  "Each title is the one a design's drawn panel prints (DW-111: a drawn panel wins over a spec table). A labelled group's rows (the export's 'Actions › Sign in') are filed under the title the panel prints ('Sign in'), never under the group or a note about the row ('(repeater)', 'in returned panel'). A title no frame draws — a row the export only specifies, such as a1's 'Nav children' — is the spec's word, kept until a frame draws the row.",
  "One panel prints one title once, its accordions' titles included (R-13). Where the export's titles would repeat: a setting beside a field of the same title keeps its title and the field gives way, taking a title of its own, as the export does in A29–A31 ('Eyebrow text' beside an 'Eyebrow' setting) and A22 #1 does ('Blurb text'); two settings, or a setting and its accordion, take the export's own other title for one of them — A4 #9's button style, drawn 'Primary action' beside its Primary action toggle, is filed as 'Action style' (A6's word). Every such title is the owner's to see (R-83) in the story that builds it; DW-166 lists the repeats the export draws.",
  "A few entries are fields, not settings — an icon slot, a list, a line of text. Each is Content wherever its panel draws it, because the settings panel draws every field there.",
  "tools/check-snapshots.mjs holds every built design's setting to the entry its title names here, and fails a setting with no entry and one whose title its own frame does not draw (R-74): the story that gives a setting a title this register does not carry files it here, with its group."
 ],
